WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.877 --> 00:00:20.779
door at Ferndean was opened by John's wife, Mary, who'd been the cook at Thornfield.

2
00:00:21.819 --> 00:00:24.000
She started as if she'd seen a ghost.

3
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.882
"Is it really you, Miss Eyre, come at this late hour to this lonely place?"

4
00:00:28.902 --> 00:00:32.123
"It is indeed, Mary," I replied.

5
00:00:32.143 --> 00:00:33.844
"How are you?"

6
00:00:34.908 --> 00:00:39.351
She led me into the kitchen, where I quickly explained that I knew everything that had happened at

7
00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:44.835
Thornfield. While I removed my bonnet and shawl, I asked if I could stay the night.

8
00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:47.637
Just then the parlor bell rang.

9
00:00:47.657 --> 00:00:53.801
"When you enter the parlor," I said, "tell your master that someone wants to speak to him, but

10
00:00:53.861 --> 00:00:54.721
don't give my name."

11
00:00:54.741 --> 00:00:59.104
"I don't think he'll see you; he refuses everybody."

12
00:01:00.185 --> 00:01:04.628
When Mary returned, she said, "You're to send in your name and your business."

13
00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:09.370
She then filled a glass with water and placed it on a tray with some candles.

14
00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.811
"Is that what he rang for?"

15
00:01:12.212 --> 00:01:12.752
I asked.

16
00:01:14.573 --> 00:01:18.255
"Yes, he always has candles brought in even though he's blind."

17
00:01:18.275 --> 00:01:21.257
"Give the tray to me, and I'll take it."

18
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:25.639
The tray shook in my hands, and water spilled from the glass.

19
00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.961
My heart pounded as Mary opened the parlor door for me.

20
00:01:31.162 --> 00:01:34.464
The parlor was a gloomy room, with only a low fire burning.

21
00:01:35.656 --> 00:01:40.400
Mr. Rochester leaned against the mantel while his dog, Pilot, lay off to the side.

22
00:01:41.641 --> 00:01:45.424
With a yelp Pilot bounded toward me and almost knocked the tray from my hand.

23
00:01:45.444 --> 00:01:50.228
"Lie down," I said softly, setting the tray on a table.

24
00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:52.390
I approached Mr.

25
00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.613
Rochester with the glass of water, and Pilot followed me, still excited.

26
00:01:56.633 --> 00:01:59.816
"Down, Pilot," I said again.

27
00:02:00.997 --> 00:02:02.898
Mr. Rochester took a sip of water.

28
00:02:02.918 --> 00:02:04.840
"Is that you, Mary?

29
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:06.901
"Mary's in the kitchen."

30
00:02:06.921 --> 00:02:08.622
"Who is this?

31
00:02:09.843 --> 00:02:10.543
Answer me now!"

32
00:02:10.924 --> 00:02:11.884
he ordered loudly.

33
00:02:11.904 --> 00:02:16.187
"Pilot knows me and so does Mary."

34
00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:19.750
Mr. Rochester shook his head in confusion.

35
00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.431
"What delusion has come over me?

36
00:02:23.572 --> 00:02:24.553
I must be insane."

37
00:02:24.573 --> 00:02:27.875
"No, sir, you're not insane."

38
00:02:29.056 --> 00:02:32.438
He groped the air in front of him, and I took his hand in mine.

39
00:02:32.458 --> 00:02:34.860
"These are Jane's fingers!

40
00:02:36.164 --> 00:02:37.706
If so, there must be more of her."

41
00:02:38.887 --> 00:02:40.568
He pulled me into his arms.

42
00:02:40.588 --> 00:02:45.272
"I'm all here, sir, and so glad to be near you again.

43
00:02:46.493 --> 00:02:48.455
I'll never leave you from this day forward."

44
00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:54.820
"Never? But I've often dreamed that you returned, and when I awoke the next morning, you were gone."

45
00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.222
"This is not a dream, sir.

46
00:02:58.283 --> 00:03:02.426
I'm an independent woman now and have the money to live near you forever."

47
00:03:02.446 --> 00:03:04.148
"What do you mean?"

48
00:03:06.088 --> 00:03:10.850
I explained to him about my uncle's bequest and said that I could afford to build a house

49
00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.671
nearby so that I could always take care of him.

50
00:03:14.932 --> 00:03:18.613
Of course I hoped that he would want to marry me, but I didn't mention that.

51
00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:24.035
We had supper together in the parlor, and he tried to ask me where I had been living,

52
00:03:24.415 --> 00:03:27.077
but I refused to tell him anything until the next day.

53
00:03:27.097 --> 00:03:31.999
"Just tell me one thing," he said as I started up the stairs for the night.

54
00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:35.400
"Were there only ladies in the house where you've been?"

55
00:03:36.592 --> 00:03:40.934
I laughed as I ran upstairs because now I would have a way to tease him out of

56
00:03:40.974 --> 00:03:41.854
his melancholy.

57
00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:47.517
We spent most of the next morning outside, and I told him about the past year.

58
00:03:48.737 --> 00:03:52.659
I left out much of what happened the first three days because I didn't want to inflict any

59
00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:53.800
unnecessary pain.

60
00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.761
The little I did say hurt him more than I would have wished.

61
00:03:58.922 --> 00:04:03.044
He said he would have given me half his fortune without demanding so much as a kiss in

62
00:04:03.084 --> 00:04:09.348
return. I then went on to tell him about Moor House and my position as schoolmistress.

63
00:04:09.368 --> 00:04:11.589
"Your cousin St.

64
00:04:11.609 --> 00:04:12.530
John," Mr.

65
00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.391
Rochester said.

66
00:04:13.411 --> 00:04:18.255
"I assume he's an older man who took little notice of you?"

67
00:04:18.275 --> 00:04:22.359
"Actually, he's not yet thirty and quite handsome.

68
00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.942
We spent a lot of time together because he was teaching me Hindustani."

69
00:04:28.224 --> 00:04:29.565
"What use could that be to you?"

70
00:04:29.585 --> 00:04:33.028
"He wanted me to go to India as his wife."

71
00:04:34.228 --> 00:04:38.329
"You must go your own way with the husband you have chosen—this St.

72
00:04:38.369 --> 00:04:39.890
John Rivers," Mr.

73
00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.070
Rochester insisted.

74
00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:45.591
I could see that my plan to make him jealous had succeeded.

75
00:04:45.611 --> 00:04:49.132
"But he doesn't love me, and I don't love him.

76
00:04:49.152 --> 00:04:51.133
I love you."

77
00:04:52.293 --> 00:04:54.173
He smiled as I clung to his neck.

78
00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.554
"And I love you, Jane.

79
00:04:57.614 --> 00:04:58.435
Will you marry me?"

80
00:04:58.455 --> 00:05:00.455
"Yes, sir."

81
00:05:02.416 --> 00:05:07.731
He kissed me and then said, "It's odd to be so happy now when I felt so desperate

82
00:05:07.771 --> 00:05:08.551
just the other night.

83
00:05:09.652 --> 00:05:13.654
I missed you so much that I called out your name, and the strangest thing was that I

84
00:05:13.694 --> 00:05:14.875
thought I heard you reply."

85
00:05:15.976 --> 00:05:18.497
Remembering the voice I'd heard, I smiled.

86
00:05:19.598 --> 00:05:21.319
Then I took his hand and kissed it.

87
00:05:22.479 --> 00:05:24.641
Reader, I married him.

88
00:05:25.962 --> 00:05:29.664
After a quiet wedding ceremony, we returned to Ferndean.

89
00:05:31.004 --> 00:05:34.265
In the kitchen I announced to Mary and John that I had married Mr.

90
00:05:34.325 --> 00:05:41.047
Rochester. Both servants approved of the match, as did Diana and Mary when I wrote to them.

91
00:05:42.327 --> 00:05:43.208
I don't know how St.

92
00:05:43.228 --> 00:05:46.849
John reacted to the news because he never answered the letter I sent him.

93
00:05:48.129 --> 00:05:51.050
Six months later he wrote to me without mentioning Mr.

94
00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.670
Rochester or my marriage.

95
00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:55.631
As for Adele I went to visit her at school.

96
00:05:56.892 --> 00:06:01.770
She looked pale and thin, and I realized that the school was too strict for a child of

97
00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:02.351
her age.

98
00:06:04.292 --> 00:06:10.117
I took her home with me, intending to be her governess, but soon discovered that my husband needed

99
00:06:10.317 --> 00:06:11.237
all my attention.

100
00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:18.203
I found Adele a more suitable school nearby, and she grew to be a pleasing and kind companion.

101
00:06:19.363 --> 00:06:24.747
I have now been married ten years, and no woman has ever been closer to her husband than

102
00:06:24.928 --> 00:06:25.248
I am.

103
00:06:26.484 --> 00:06:32.686
Mr. Rochester continued to be blind for the first two years of our marriage, but gradually regained some

104
00:06:32.786 --> 00:06:33.686
sight in his eye.

105
00:06:34.806 --> 00:06:40.168
When his first-born child was put into his arms, he could see that the boy had inherited his

106
00:06:40.428 --> 00:06:44.629
eyes as they once were—large, brilliant, and black.

107
00:06:45.789 --> 00:06:48.070
Diana and Mary are both happily married.

108
00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:52.731
Diana's husband is a captain in the navy, and Mary's is a clergyman.

109
00:06:53.911 --> 00:06:56.172
We continue to see them on a regular basis.

110
00:06:57.444 --> 00:06:58.024
As for St.

111
00:06:58.064 --> 00:07:03.907
John, he followed his intended path and became a missionary in India, but he never married.

112
00:07:05.107 --> 00:07:11.890
Thus Edward and I are happy, and all the more so because those we love are happy too.
